[Music]  this is what remains of a un logistics  base in goma in north kivu province  thousands of congolese protesters  chanted anti-un's slogans demanding the  peacekeeping mission leave the country  they threw stones looted office  equipment and other material  even the peacekeepers stationed inside  and local police could not control the  crowd  [Music]  people are dying every day in the north  in beni and in ituri province in the  presence of monasco  the peacekeepers have said they are  unable to keep people safe to ensure the  continued implementation the deputy  spokesman for the un mission says  everything is being done to minimize  disruption to its work the mission is  activating additional security protocols  and advancing contingency planning to  ensure the continued implementation of  its mandate and the secure the safety  and security of all un personnel  the relationship between some congolese  and the un has been tense at best the  protesters say the un has failed to  protect them from frequent attacks  the u.n peacekeeping mission in the  democratic republic of congo has heard a  presence here for more than 20 years  despite this more than a hundred rebel  groups in the east control the vast  region that is rich in minerals  we will respect our commitment with  monucco but we should also avoid any  speech or declarations likely to create  mistrust  such altercations are not new in 2019  there were riots in the territory of  beni several people were killed and un  property was destroyed to this date  residency the u.n the national army and  other foreign troops have failed to stop  the violence  many congolese say they are tired they  want peace and if the u.n cannot provide  stability than its forces need to leave  catherine soy al jazeera

